        <mxCell id="legend" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F8FC;strokeColor=#7FA6C9;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#12345A;fontSize=15;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" value="&lt;b&gt;Relationship guide&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1 : 1 = one-to-one &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;1 : 0..1&lt;/b&gt; = optional zero-or-one &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;1 : M&lt;/b&gt; = one-to-many &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; | &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;M : N&lt;/b&gt; = many-to-many&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#A86A00&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;PK&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; = Primary key &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;font color=&quot;#087E8B&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;FK&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt; = Foreign key &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;b&gt;UQ&lt;/b&gt; = Unique&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Appointment–Diagnosis is M : N, implemented using AppointmentDiagnosis.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;div&gt;The AppointmentDiagnosis table resolves the many-to-many relationship between appointments and diagnoses. PrescriptionItem links prescriptions to medicines and stores the details required for each prescribed medicine. The foreign keys connect related records, whilst the primary keys uniquely identify each record. FollowUpPlan.AppointmentID is unique, allowing an appointment to have at most one follow-up plan.&lt;i&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
